+# The Daily Grind
+
+Static marketing homepage for The Daily Grind Coffee Co., served with `pnpm start`
+(statikk on port 11222).
+
+## Signed receipts & gift vouchers
+
+The homepage section **Signed Receipts & Gift Vouchers** (`#receipts`) issues and
+verifies digitally signed order receipts and gift vouchers entirely in the browser.
+No build step or dependencies are required; everything runs on the Web Crypto API.
+
+| File | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `js/dg-sign.js` | Pure signing/verification library (runs in browsers and Node). |
+| `js/dg-keystore.js` | Persists the issuer key pair in IndexedDB. |
+| `js/dg-ui.js` | Wires the homepage forms, outputs and verifier. |
+| `test/dg-sign.test.mjs` | `node --test` suite covering both algorithms. |
+
+Run the tests with `npm test` (Node 24+; ML-DSA in Node's Web Crypto is still
+flagged experimental, so the script silences that warning).
+
+### Algorithms
+
+| JWS `alg` | Primitive | JWK | When used |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `ML-DSA-65` | FIPS 204 module-lattice signature (quantum-resistant) | `kty: "AKP"`, `pub` | Preferred, whenever the browser's `crypto.subtle` supports it |
+| `ES256` | ECDSA P-256 with SHA-256 | `kty: "EC"`, `crv: "P-256"` | Fallback on browsers without ML-DSA |
+
+Key selection is automatic: `generateIssuerKey()` tries the algorithms in the
+order above and keeps the first that works. The private key is generated
+**non-extractable**, so its bytes can never be read by page script. It is stored
+in IndexedDB as an opaque `CryptoKey` handle so it survives reloads.
+
+### Token format
+
+Documents are JWS Compact Serialization (RFC 7515):
+
+```
+base64url(header) . base64url(payload) . base64url(signature)
+```
+
+Header:
+
+```json
+{ "alg": "ML-DSA-65", "typ": "dg-receipt+jws", "kid": "<RFC 7638 JWK thumbprint>" }
+```
+
+`typ` is `dg-receipt+jws` or `dg-voucher+jws` and must agree with `payload.type`.
+
+Receipt payload (money is in integer cents):
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "receipt",
+  "iss": "the-daily-grind",
+  "orderId": "DG-20261028-3F9A1C",
+  "store": "Main St. Roastery",
+  "currency": "USD",
+  "items": [{ "name": "Maple Oat Latte", "qty": 2, "unitPrice": 575 }],
+  "total": 1150,
+  "issuedAt": "2026-10-28T09:12:44.000Z",
+  "customer": "Alex"
+}
+```
+
+Voucher payload:
+
+```json
+{
+  "type": "voucher",
+  "iss": "the-daily-grind",
+  "code": "DG-K7PQ-2MNA-9XTB",
+  "amount": 2500,
+  "currency": "USD",
+  "issuedAt": "2026-10-28T09:12:44.000Z",
+  "expiresAt": "2027-10-28T09:12:44.000Z",
+  "recipient": "Jordan",
+  "message": "Happy birthday!"
+}
+```
+
+### Verification rules
+
+`verifyToken(token, trustedKeys)` returns `{ ok, status, reason, signatureValid, header, payload }`
+where `status` is `valid`, `expired` or `invalid`. It never throws on bad input. A
+token is accepted only if all of the following hold:
+
+1. It parses as three non-empty base64url segments with JSON header and payload.
+2. `header.kid` names one of the supplied trusted public keys. Unknown keys are
+   rejected, so only documents from The Daily Grind's key holders pass.
+3. The algorithm used for verification is the one bound to the **trusted key**,
+   and it must equal `header.alg`. A token cannot downgrade or swap algorithms
+   (`none`, `HS256`, ES256↔ML-DSA, …).
+4. `crit` is absent and `typ` is one of the two known document types.
+5. The signature verifies over the exact `header.payload` bytes received, so any
+   change to any field invalidates it.
+6. The payload matches the document schema (`iss`, order id / voucher code
+   formats, integer money, totals equal to the sum of line items, ISO dates).
+7. Vouchers whose `expiresAt` has passed report `status: "expired"` with
+   `signatureValid: true`, distinguishing a genuine-but-expired voucher from a forgery.
+
+### Sharing the public key
+
+"Copy public key" / "Download public key set" export the issuer's public JWK (plus
+any rotated-out keys as a JWK Set). Paste it into the verifier's *Trusted issuer
+public keys* box on another device to verify documents issued here. Private keys
+are refused by the importer.
+
+Rotating the key keeps the previous public keys in the trusted list so older
+receipts and vouchers continue to verify locally.
